  "chinamo": {
    "name": "Chinamo",
    "note": [
      "REDRAWN FROM A PHOTOGRAPH of the real thing on the Paseo, and almost",
      "nothing of the first guess survived. It was built as a lone booth with a",
      "red-and-cream striped awning and a hand-painted board. What is actually",
      "there is:",
      "  * ONE CONTINUOUS ROW. The chinamos share a frame and run off into the",
      "    distance; they are not separate stalls with gaps. So the three are",
      "    placed CONTIGUOUSLY in content.py and each draws a module wide enough",
      "    to butt against its neighbours.",
      "  * A CORRUGATED ZINC ROOF, dark and ribbed, on a slight pitch — not a",
      "    striped awning and not canvas. (Some rows are blue sponsored tarp",
      "    instead; `roofStyle` switches, and `tarp` is still in the catalog.)",
      "  * THE BANNER FASCIA IS THE WHOLE LOOK, and it is the thing the first",
      "    version missed completely. A continuous band of printed panels —",
      "    dark purple ground, huge saturated lettering, photographs of the food",
      "    itself — running above the counter AND down its front. CHURROS",
      "    RELLENOS, MANZANA ESCARCHADA, ALGODÓN DE AZÚCAR. From above, that",
      "    bright band along the front edge IS the chinamo.",
      "  * Glass cases and stainless counters between the panels.",
      "Seen from above — which is how this game sees everything — that reads as",
      "the dark ribbed roof, the printed band along its front edge, and the",
      "serving counter in front of that."
    ],
    "parts": [
      {
        "shape": "zinc",
        "w": 1.9,
        "h": 0.8,
        "ribs": 13,
        "fill": "#3a3b42",
        "rib": "#4d4f58",
